{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (orchestrator) submitted a stitch task (#5190) to implement error handling and edge cases for `cmd/nproc` per srd046-nproc requirements R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3. The specific requirements are:\n   - R2.1: If any positional operand is provided, print error to stderr and exit 1\n   - R2.2: If --ignore is given a non-numeric value, print error to stderr and exit 1\n   - R2.3: Unknown flags must produce error to stderr and exit 1\n   \n   Design decisions: D1 = preserve existing R1.1-R1.4 implementation unchanged; D2 = error messages go to stderr, match GNU nproc format and exit codes.\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (compiles), AC2-AC4 (R2.1-R2.3 behaviors functional), AC5 (go vet clean).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU coreutils `nproc` utility\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binary (`gnproc`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Manual flag parsing (no cobra for this simple utility)\n   - Error messages to stderr matching GNU format\n   - SPDX copyright headers required on all Go files\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - Build to `bin/` directory: `go build -o bin/nproc ./cmd/nproc/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd046-nproc.yaml** (Read, for understanding requirements)\n     - Defines R1 (default behavior/flags) and R2 (error handling) requirement groups\n     - R2.1: positional operands → error + exit 1\n     - R2.2: non-numeric --ignore value → error + exit 1  \n     - R2.3: unknown flags → error + exit 1\n     - Non-goals: no CPU affinity, no cgroup limits on macOS\n\n   - **cmd/nproc/main.go** (Read, this is the file to modify)\n     - Current implementation covers R1.1-R1.4 (from task #5188)\n     - Already has SIGPIPE handler, manual arg parsing loop\n     - Notable: `_ = allFlag` on line 71 — the --all flag is parsed but discarded (both available and installed counts are the same on macOS per non_goals)\n     - Already has parseIgnore helper function for --ignore value validation\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd046-nproc R1.1-R1.4.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"runtime\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n     \n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     \n         allFlag := false\n         ignoreN := 0\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n     \n         for len(args) > 0 {\n             arg := args[0]\n             args = args[1:]\n     \n             if arg == \"--\" {\n                 break\n             }\n             if arg == \"--all\" {\n                 allFlag = true\n                 continue\n             }\n             if arg == \"--ignore\" {\n                 if len(args) == 0 {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: option '--ignore' requires an argument\\n\")\n                     fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'nproc --help' for more information.\")\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 if !parseIgnore(args[0], &ignoreN) {\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 args = args[1:]\n                 continue\n             }\n             if strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--ignore=\") {\n                 val := arg[len(\"--ignore=\"):]\n                 if !parseIgnore(val, &ignoreN) {\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 continue\n             }\n             if strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && len(arg) > 1 {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", arg)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'nproc --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: extra operand '%s'\\n\", arg)\n             fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'nproc --help' for more information.\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     \n         for _, arg := range args {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: extra operand '%s'\\n\", arg)\n             fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'nproc --help' for more information.\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     \n         count := runtime.NumCPU()\n         _ = allFlag\n     \n         count -= ignoreN\n         if count < 1 {\n             count = 1\n         }\n     \n         if _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, count); err != nil {\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func parseIgnore(val string, n *int) bool {\n         v, err := strconv.Atoi(val)\n         if err != nil || v < 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: invalid number: '%s'\\n\", val)\n             return false\n         }\n         *n = v\n         return true\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. I only read two files before being interrupted for summarization.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The existing code in cmd/nproc/main.go appears to already implement R2.1 (extra operand rejection), R2.2 (non-numeric --ignore rejection via parseIgnore), and R2.3 (unknown flag rejection) to some degree. However, I need to carefully verify these match GNU nproc behavior exactly and potentially fix edge cases. One concern: `parseIgnore` rejects negative values (`v < 0`), but GNU nproc may accept `--ignore=-1`. This is potentially an R1.3 concern though, not R2.2. The task package comment should be updated to include R2.1-R2.3 references.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial massive task description providing full project context, SRDs, constitutions, and the specific stitch task #5190 for implementing srd046-nproc R2.1-R2.3 error handling\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Analyze whether existing R2.1-R2.3 implementations are complete and correct\n   - Make any necessary modifications to cmd/nproc/main.go\n   - Update the package doc comment to reference R2.1-R2.3 (currently only says R1.1-R1.4)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/nproc ./cmd/nproc/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/nproc/` to verify no issues (AC5)\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria AC1-AC5\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading both required files (the SRD spec and the existing main.go) and was about to analyze and implement the necessary changes. I was interrupted immediately after the two Read calls returned. The next action would be to determine what modifications (if any) are needed to cmd/nproc/main.go for R2.1-R2.3, make those changes, then verify compilation and tests.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Modify `cmd/nproc/main.go` to ensure R2.1-R2.3 are properly implemented. At minimum, update the package doc comment from `// Implements srd046-nproc R1.1-R1.4.` to `// Implements srd046-nproc R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3.` Then verify the error handling logic matches GNU nproc behavior exactly — particularly checking if `parseIgnore` correctly handles all non-numeric cases for R2.2. Then run `go build -o bin/nproc ./cmd/nproc/` and `go vet ./cmd/nproc/` to satisfy AC1 and AC5. The task description states: \"Implement srd046-nproc R2.1 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd046-nproc R2.2 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd046-nproc R2.3 per the SRD specification\" with design decision D1: \"Preserve the existing R1.1-R1.4 implementation unchanged; add R2.x behaviors without breaking existing functionality.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generate