{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01M9uggZH4vSfJZae51VFqXK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the existing code, R2.1-R2.3 are already implemented in the current main.go:\n\n- R2.1 (positional operands → error + exit 1): Lines 59-61 handle non-flag arguments as \"extra operand\", and lines 64-68 handle operands after `--`.\n- R2.2 (non-numeric --ignore → error + exit 1): The `parseIgnore` function on lines 83-90 handles this.\n- R2.3 (unknown flags → error + exit 1): Lines 54-58 handle unknown flags starting with `-`.\n\n\nI need to update the package doc comment to reference R2.1-R2.3 and verify the error message format matches GNU nproc exactly. I'm also reconsidering the `parseIgnore` function—it currently rejects negative values, but I should check whether GNU nproc actually accepts them or treats them as errors like non-numeric input. The current implementation rejects negative numbers too (`v < 0`). But negative numbers ARE numeric - they're just negative. GNU nproc accepts `--ignore=-1` and treats it as subtracting -1 (adding 1). So `parseIgnore` rejecting `v < 0` might be wrong.\n\nWait, but `strconv.Atoi` will parse \"-1\" as -1 successfully, and then `v < 0` check would reject it. But GNU nproc does accept `--ignore=-1`. Let me think... Actually the task says D1: \"Preserve the existing R1.1-R1.4 implementation unchanged.\" So I shouldn't modify the parseIgnore behavior if it was part of R1.x implementation.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the parseIgnore function was part of R1.3/R1.4 implementation (handling --ignore=N). The R2.2 requirement is specifically about non-numeric values. A negative number is still numeric, so rejecting it under R2.2 would be incorrect.\n\nBut I need to check what GNU nproc actually does with `--ignore=-1`. If it rejects it, then the current behavior is correct (even if the reason is technically R1.3 not R2.2). If it accepts it, then we have a bug in R1.3 that I shouldn't fix here since D1 says preserve R1.x unchanged. I should just focus on updating the package doc comment and verifying the existing R2.x implementations are correct.\n\nNow I'm building and testing the changes to make sure everything compiles and the doc comment is accurate.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12100,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12100},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e465fd2f-7ba5-4e37-9549-c54faa6b5f4b","uuid":"ef906920-dbc0-4b8c-a3d4-31ae73494e56"}
